<a name="2026-10-29-brazils-election"> </a>
<h3>Brazil’s election</h3>
<p>Here is the <a href="AI/2026-10-28-Brazil.html">best  summary</a> 
I
 have seen of what’s going on in Brazil right after the leftist
 candidate Lula won the election.
<p>To summarize, it looks like both Lula and Bolsonaro are really
 corrupt. As soon as Lula won, they told Bolsonaro to give up his
 passports. He responded by fleeing Brazil with his family and coming to
 the US to seek political asylum.
<p>The fact that Bolsonaro was asked to give up his passports as soon as
 the leftists secured victory in Brazil looks like political prosecution
 to me, even if Bolsonaro is guilty of all the charges being levied
 against him.
<p>The leftists do not support Bolsonaro’s politial asylum. To summarize
 the general tone of leftists, one leftist posted on left-wing social
 media that “<a href="https://archive.ph/UZKbz#selection-6659.0-6659.88">It will be up to a Democratic  administration to ensure that this criminal faces  justice</a>”. 
Another leftist posted, again on left-wing social media, that “<a href="https://archive.ph/aa9v2#selection-4109.0-4109.56">Interesting how this criminal asylum seeker was  approved</a>”. 
Even the
 left-wing mainstream media has <a href="AI/2026-10-28-BrazilNYT.html">joined the  fray</a>, 
mentioning Bolsonaro’s crimes and highlighting his
 ties to the Trump administration, while not mentioning Lula’s crimes.
<a name="2026-10-29-the-myth-of-chad"> </a>
<h3>The myth of “Chad”</h3>
<p>Here is <a href="AI/2026-10-27-ChadMyth.html">yet another refutation of the myth of  “Chad”</a>. 
“Chad” is an
 imaginary man who magically makes lots of women want to have sex with
 him. In the imagination of some, this “Chad” gets all the women,
 leaving most men without sex. I discuss why this is a myth in <a href="80-20-myth.html">a long article</a>. 
And, no, <a href="https://datepsychology.com/is-self-reported-sexual-partner-data-accurate/">women are lot lying in those  surveys</a> 
(<a href="https://archive.ph/CzjdF">archive link</a>).
